      "message": "[error] Line 619: 🔴 `followPeerTransport()` acquires `callMutex_` and then calls `isRetiredSipTransport()`, which now also acquires `callMutex_`. Because this mutex is non-recursive, this can self-deadlock on the probe path and stall recovery handling. Fix by splitting `isRetiredSipTransport` into a `_Locked` helper that assumes the mutex is already held (or by checking `abandonedTransports_` directly inside `followPeerTransport`), and keep a separate externally-locking wrapper for callers that do not already hold the lock.",
